{
  "country": "United States of America",
  "iso3": "USA",
  "period": "FY2006\u2013FY2025 (all 20 years: actual outlays; FY2026\u2013FY2031 estimates in the OMB vintage excluded)",
  "sources": [
    "OMB Historical Tables Table 3.2 (Outlays by Function and Subfunction), FY2027 vintage (released Apr 2026), downloaded as xlsx from https://www.whitehouse.gov/omb/information-resources/budget/historical-tables/ on Oct 9, 2026",
    "OMB Historical Tables Table 1.1 used to cross-check total outlays: Table 3.2 'Total outlays' matches Table 1.1 exactly for all 20 years",
    "FX: United States of America-profile.json (fx_lcu_per_usd_annual_avg = 1.0 for USD; confirmed 2006-2025 year list)",
    "Values are in millions of dollars in the OMB tables; converted to USD billions here"
  ],
  "category_mapping": {
    "defense": "Function 050 National Defense (total)",
    "health": "Function 550 Health (total) + Function 570 Medicare (total) + subfunction 703 Hospital and medical care for veterans (veterans health care moved here; see notes)",
    "education": "Function 500 Education, Training, Employment, and Social Services (total) + subfunction 702 Veterans education, training, and rehabilitation. Note: Function 500 includes training/employment and social services beyond schooling",
    "social_protection": "Function 600 Income Security (total) + Function 650 Social Security (total) + veterans subfunctions 701 Income security for veterans + 704 Veterans housing + 705 Other veterans benefits and services (see notes)",
    "economic_affairs": "Functions 250 General Science, Space and Technology + 270 Energy + 300 Natural Resources and Environment (including 304 Pollution control and abatement - environment kept here, see notes) + 350 Agriculture + 370 Commerce and Housing Credit + 400 Transportation + 450 Community and Regional Development",
    "general_admin": "Function 800 General Government (total); excludes net interest (Function 900)",
    "debt_interest": "Function 900 Net Interest (total; interest paid net of interest received by trust funds)",
    "public_order": "Function 750 Administration of Justice (total: federal law enforcement, litigation/judicial, corrections, criminal justice assistance)",
    "other": "Function 150 International Affairs (total) + Function 920 Allowances (dotted/not applicable in actual years - treated as 0, see notes) + Function 950 Undistributed Offsetting Receipts (negative values; netted into 'other', see notes)"
  },
  "fiscal_year_note": "US federal fiscal year runs October\u2013September; FY2023 = Oct 2022\u2013Sep 2023.",
  "notes": [
    "Veterans Benefits and Services (Function 700) split by purpose rather than kept whole: 703 veterans hospital/medical care -> health; 702 veterans education/training/rehabilitation -> education; 701 income security, 704 veterans housing, 705 other veterans benefits -> social_protection. The five subfunctions sum exactly to Function 700 total each year (verified).",
    "Environment: Function 300 (Natural Resources and Environment), including subfunction 304 Pollution control and abatement, kept in economic_affairs as natural-resources/economic-affairs spending rather than a separate environment line.",
    "Allowances (Function 920): OMB marks these cells '...........' (not applicable) for all actual years; only the estimates contain allowances. Treated as 0 in the 'other' aggregation.",
    "Undistributed offsetting receipts (Function 950) are negative receipts netted against outlays; they are kept inside 'other', so 'other' is reduced accordingly (e.g. FY2025: $45.2bn international affairs, -$150.3bn offsetting receipts).",
    "FY2026\u2013FY2031 in this OMB vintage are labeled estimates and are excluded; every year in this file is actual outlays.",
    "All 20 years: sum of the 9 area components (unrounded) equals total outlays exactly; pct shares rounded to 1 decimal.",
    "No estimated or imputed values: no area uses estimated:true.",
    "Medicare = subfunction 571 total; Social Security = subfunction 651 total (single-line functions; values sit on the subfunction rows)."
  ],
  "unit": "percent of total federal outlays; USD billions",
